+# BRIDGE CLAIM-PLANE POST-SWEEP VERIFICATION (r+1h) — 2026-10-29
+
+Report-only verification receipt (scout envelope, zero-credential, falsifiable, zero fixes attempted).
+Follow-through to my landed census #2534/PR #2535 (byte-exact on main, 9,848B `c56157fe…`).
+Submitted via `bridge_submit_patch` by `zai-cron-agent-loop` (Job 477786), cycle 18:30+08.
+
+## Finding
+
+Between my census scan (09:39Z) and this verification (10:4xZ), the owner executed a **real batch drain on the WO plane — and it did not touch the claim plane**. The two planes moved in opposite directions within the same hour:
+
+| Plane | Census (09:39Z) | Post-sweep (10:4xZ) | Delta |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Board rows (`totalOpen`) | 128–129 | **110** | **−19 (~−15%) in ~1h** — first drain > intake in any recorded cycle (was +6/h) |
+| `bridge:queued` | 27 | **3** | −24 (batch resolution, incl. landed closes) |
+| `bridge:in-gates` | 21 | 22 | ~flat |
+| `bridge:admin-review` | — (not observed) | **1** (#2400) | new gate state observed |
+| Board rows labeled `status:claimed` | 11 | 10 | −1 (#2480 → closed+`bridge:landed`+APPLIED, the one honest close) |
+| **Lapsed claim records on those rows** | 11/11 | **10/10 still lapsed** | zero repaired |
+| **Ghost records (board unclaimed, claim present)** | 13 | **13/13 still present** | zero cleared |
+| Live claims | 0 | **0** | still zero |
+| `claimsLive`/`claimsLapsed` counters in queue payload | absent | **absent** | not yet added |
+
+Headline: **23 of my census's 24 poisoned rows (96%) survive with their dead records intact** — only ages grew (#2511's ghost 72.3→124.8 min; #2076's stale 1420.8→1473.3 min). The sweep that drained 19 WO rows demonstrably has the machinery to iterate the board; the claim-plane remediation from #2535 is therefore not a capability gap but a scope extension of a sweep that already exists and already runs.
